# Remote access runbook worksheet

Fill one copy per planned access or per automation identity. Remote access to
shared or production systems is an operator action: the reviewer prepares and
checks this worksheet, the named operator performs and records the access.

## Request

- Change or incident ID: <ID>
- Purpose (one sentence): <what must be done remotely, and why it cannot be done through the deployment pipeline>
- Target hosts or resources: <names, environment>
- Requested by / approved by: <name> / <name, date>
- Operator performing the access: <name>
- Window: <start - end, time zone>

## Access path

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Method | Bastion and ProxyJump / Azure Bastion / just-in-time port opening / session manager / other |
| Entry point | <bastion host or managed service> |
| Network rule opened, and when it closes | <rule, expiry> |
| Host key or host certificate verification | <known_hosts entry, @cert-authority line, or managed> |
| Session recording or audit log location | <where, retention> |

## Credentials

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Key type | ed25519 with passphrase, or hardware-backed (`-sk`) key |
| Certificate | Principal <name>, validity <for example 8h>, serial <n> |
| Agent | Local agent only; no agent forwarding |
| Privilege on target | <account>, escalation through sudo with logging |

Never paste private keys, passphrases, or tokens into this worksheet, tickets,
chat, or version control.

## Plan

| Step | Command or action | Expected result | Rollback |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | | | |
| 2 | | | |

Run read-only inspection first. State-changing commands need the approval
above and a tested rollback.

## Automation identity (when a pipeline or tool connects)

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Identity and owner | <service principal, deploy key, or certificate principal> |
| Allowed commands | `command=` restriction, forced command, or sudo rule |
| Source restriction | `from=` pattern or network rule |
| Forwarding | `restrict` option on the authorized key, or certificate without extensions |
| Credential lifetime and rotation | <for example certificate valid 1h, issued per run> |
| Secret storage | <secret store name; never the repository> |

## Close-out

- [ ] Temporary network rules and just-in-time grants removed or expired.
- [ ] Short-lived certificates expired; any long-lived key used is rotated or revoked.
- [ ] Session log and command history attached to the change record.
- [ ] Unexpected findings raised as follow-up items with owners.
- [ ] Host key changes, if any, explained and distributed.

## Sign-off

- Operator: <name, date>
- Reviewer: <name, date>
